TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Traced checkpoint cp-smoke's exit 1 to a stdin-plumbing defect in scripts/run-smoke.sh, not to any probe logic: the podman invocation at scripts/run-smoke.sh:10 omits -i, so the heredoc body never reaches the container's `python3 -`. Evidence: (1) the capture for this attempt (/home/tom/.local/state/tally/capture/archive/01a051b2-032b-70c0-af16-724b46f58392.cp-smoke/checkpoint.json) contains exactly one stdout line, the trailing `smoke receipt: ...` echo, and zero container stdout even though the embedded program unconditionally prints `json.dumps(r, indent=1)`; stderr is empty, so no probe ever raised. (2) No receipt exists anywhere in the worktree: results/receipts/ holds build.json, weights-coordinator.json, weights-worker.json and no smoke.json, and results/receipts/failed/ was never created, so the container wrote nothing at all. (3) The trailing validator then exits 1 solely because results/receipts/smoke.json is absent — that is the observed exit code, with a clean `git status` and head == baseRev 6e818349eeb947501ac04ba83e826764a042011c. (4) Reproduced the mechanism directly: `podman run --rm docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04 cat - <<EOF` prints nothing, while the same command with -i prints the heredoc line; podman does not attach stdin without -i or -a stdin, so `python3 -` reads an empty program, does nothing, and exits 0 under set -euo pipefail. (5) This is not a regression from the authorized fix: `git log -- scripts/run-smoke.sh` shows the podman line has lacked -i in all four revisions (9a31e0b, 520f24b, 9480958, 7509202), and all four archived cp-smoke captures (01a05114, 01a05128, 01a05150, 01a051b2) show the byte-identical single-line stdout and exit 1. The admission-probe TypeError repaired at 7509202 was found by manual in-container repro and is real, but it could never have been reached by the checkpoint command itself, so steering notes 6 and 8 authorized a retry against a cause that was not the one firing here. Nothing in the container, the GPU aperture, or the image is implicated: localhost/flashnext:dev exists and cp-build passed. The fix is a one-token source edit outside this checkpoint's authority — checkpoints must not modify the repository and never retry — hence blocked. Note the identical defect in scripts/make-proxy.sh:116, whose heredoc-to-`python3 -` invocation also omits -i and will fail the same silent way when the proxy checkpoint runs.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","goal":"Make the container heredocs actually execute. In scripts/run-smoke.sh, add -i (or -a stdin) to the `podman run` invocation on line 10 so the `python3 -` heredoc body is delivered to the container; apply the same fix to the `podman run` invocation at scripts/make-proxy.sh:116, which has the identical silent-no-op defect. Add no other behavioral change: the five probes (arch, fp8_cast, registry, aperture, admission), the D12 failed/ quarantine, the receipt-restore purity guard, and the trailing validator all stay as written. After the fix, `bash scripts/run-smoke.sh` must run the probes in-container, print the receipt JSON, land results/receipts/smoke.json with status pass (or a fail receipt under results/receipts/failed/ if a probe genuinely fails), and exit 0; a second run over the already-correct base must leave every tracked file byte-identical per the checkpoint-purity note. Commit the receipt inside the lane commit so the later cp-smoke checkpoint re-run is a pure validator.","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh","scripts/make-proxy.sh","results/receipts/smoke.json"],"dependencies":["cp-build"],"acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"heredoc-reaches-container","description":"The smoke script's podman invocation attaches stdin, so the heredoc program is delivered to the container instead of being discarded.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -n 'podman run' scripts/run-smoke.sh | grep -Eq -- ' (-i|--interactive|-a stdin)( |$)'"]},{"id":"smoke-runs-and-passes","description":"scripts/run-smoke.sh executes the five probes in-container and exits 0.","argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"pass-receipt-present","description":"results/receipts/smoke.json exists with status pass and records all five probes.","argv":["python3","-c","import json;d=json.load(open('results/receipts/smoke.json'));assert d['status']=='pass',d;assert set(d['data'])>={'arch','fp8_cast','registry','aperture','admission'},d"]},{"id":"rerun-is-pure","description":"A second run over the already-correct base leaves every tracked file byte-identical, satisfying the checkpoint-purity contract.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/run-smoke.sh && git diff --quiet && git diff --cached --quiet"]},{"id":"proxy-builder-stdin-fixed","description":"scripts/make-proxy.sh's podman invocation also attaches stdin, so its heredoc is not silently discarded.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -n 'podman run' scripts/make-proxy.sh | grep -Eq -- ' (-i|--interactive|-a stdin)( |$)'"]}]}}
